    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-051 — viewport units (vh/vw/vmin/vmax).** Two commits. **Third commit (docs) follows after merge.**\n\nCloses a gap that `calc(100vh - 48px)` required: the sticky sidebar's `max-height` rule that ADR-050 surfaced as still-unresolved.\n\n## What shipped\n\n### Commit 1 — `parse_length` + `parse_operand` (`fcf06e5`)\n\n- `LengthContext` gains `viewport_w`, `viewport_h` (defaults 0)\n- `parse_length` handles `vh`/`vw`/`vmin`/`vmax`\n- **`parse_operand` (math expression parser) gains 4 matching branches** — the real fix. `parse_operand` had its own inline unit classification separate from `parse_length`, so `calc(100vh - 48px)` returned 0 until both paths learned viewport units.\n- One existing test updated in place: `\"calc: unknown unit (vh) yields zero\"` → `\"calc: vh resolves via viewport_h (ADR-051)\"`, assertion `0.0f → -48.0f` (correct when `viewport_h=0`: `100vh=0`, minus 48 = -48).\n\n### Commit 2 — Threading + 18 tests (`770686a`)\n\n- `layout()` / `layout_with_pseudo()` gain `viewport_height` param (default 0.0f)\n- `layout_element()` gains `viewport_w`, `viewport_h` params\n- 7 internal `layout_element` call sites updated\n- 4 in-scope `LengthContext` sites populated; 3 out-of-scope sites documented as deferrals\n- `render_pipeline.cpp` passes `0.0f` for `viewport_height` (GTK height not in scope; documented deferral)\n- `run()` / `run_with_ua()` in `test_layout.cpp` extended with `viewport_height`\n- 18 tests: direct vh/vw/vmin/vmax, `calc()` combinations, padding/border/margin with viewport units, existing `%`/`px`/`em`/`rem` regressions, `min()` of vh + px\n\n## The decisive smoke test (Commit 1, 14 cases)\n\n```\n100vh                          -> 800.0\n50vh                           -> 400.0\n100vw                          -> 1774.0\n50vw                           -> 887.0\n100vmin                        -> 800.0\n100vmax                        -> 1774.0\ncalc(100vh - 48px)             -> 752.0   (was 0)\ncalc(50vw + 50px)              -> 937.0   (was 0)\nmin(50vw, 800px)               -> 800.0   (was 0)\nmax(50vw, 800px)               -> 887.0   (was 0)\n100px / 2em / 1rem / 50%       -> unchanged\ncalc(50% + 10px)               -> 210.0   unchanged\ncalc(100vh - 48px) vh=0        -> -48.0   (mathematically correct)\n```\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero first-viewport PNG delta in production**: `render_pipeline.cpp` passes `viewport_height=0`. Every `vh`/`vw` rule in Wikipedia CSS resolves to 0, exactly as it did pre-ADR-051.\n\n**The value is empirical, not visual**:\n- `parse_length(\"calc(100vh - 48px)\", viewport_h=800)` returns 752 (was 0)\n- When GTK height threading lands (future ADR), `.vector-sticky-pinned-container`'s `max-height` gets a real value automatically — no ADR-051 code change needed\n- All tests construct `LengthContext` with explicit viewport dims and verify correct resolution\n\n## What this unblocks\n\n**`position: sticky`** — sticky's remaining prerequisite after ADR-051 is scroll-Y threading (separate cycle). `100vh` resolving is one of two prerequisites.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- `scroll-margin-top` property (unparsed)\n- `svh` / `lvh` / `dvh` (0 uses in target)\n- Percentage `max-height` (needs `parent_content_height` threading)\n- `max-height` / `max-width` honoring in layout (separate min/max clamp ADR)\n- GTK allocated height threading to `render_pipeline`\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-051: 626 / 2407\n- After Commit 1: 626 / 2407 (one test updated in place)\n- After Commit 2: **644 / 2465** (+18 / +58)\n\nRefs #234\n",
